      "raw_locator": [
        {
          "book": "2KI",
          "chapter": 3,
          "verse": 25
        }
      ],
      "en": "They beat down the cities; and on every good piece of land each man cast his stone, and filled it. They also stopped all the springs of water and cut down all the good trees, until in Kir Hareseth all they left was its stones; however the men armed with slings went around it and attacked it.",
      "ko": "그 성읍을 쳐서 헐고 각기 돌을 던져 모든 좋은 밭에 가득하게 하고 모든 샘을 메우고 모든 좋은 나무를 베고 길하레셋의 돌들은 남기고 물맷군이 두루 다니며 치니라",
      "source_text_hash": "3cd416637d785a8a0baf34a16c127198c31e214fe9232540ffdd09fdb01ec8f3",
      "translation_text_hash": "f84571ad8d16afb2abeeb32ba03d9669cc3cb06b8639e449cb3882b2e9b96e42",
